---
# Copy to `.claude/cicada-guide.local.md` in your project root and edit.
# Every key is optional; delete the ones you do not want. Keep `enabled: true`.
#
# This file is per-project and per-user. Add `.claude/*.local.md` to .gitignore.

enabled: true

# Jurisdiction to assume when a request names no state. Must be one of the
# divisions `list_states` returns — the 50 states plus DC, not territories.
default_division: Alabama

# Session to assume within that jurisdiction. Resolved through `list_sessions`.
# Left commented out so a copied template pins no session. Uncomment it and use
# a session name `list_sessions` returns, such as the current regular session.
# default_session: <session name>

# Prepended to the `context` analytics string on every tool call. Third person,
# no names, no credentials, no personal data.
context_prefix: Constituent research desk

# markdown | json — used when a request implies neither. Never sent to the tools
# without a response_format parameter: show_bill, show_person_record,
# show_official, get_rollcall_breakdown.
response_format: markdown
---

# Project context

Free text below the frontmatter is standing background for legislative research in this
project — the subject area, a time window, why the research is being done. It is folded
into scoping decisions the way a preference you restate each session would be.

It cannot lift the plugin's constraints. Federal bills, municipal ordinances, and ballot
measures are still out of the dataset; legislators are still not graded, scored, or
predicted; claims still come only from what the tools returned.

Replace this section with your own notes, or delete it.
